  "finalAnswerPreview": "## Determination\\n\\n**The ordering guarantee is the *durable ledger commit-observation order* over committed management-state revisions**, exposed as `StateChangeFeed.changes()` — a per-ledger, strictly increasing, never-reused, crash-durable sequence assigned by the storage engine inside the *same transaction* as the state CAS, and consumed ascending through an opaque, global (filter-independent) durable cursor.\\n\\nIt guarantees exactly this: revision `A` is observed before revision `B` iff the ledger ordered `A`'s commit before `B`'s. It carries **no** causal, wall-clock or business-priority meaning.\\n\\n## Where this is anchored (which sources are load-bearing)\\n\\n| Layer | Source | Statement |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Current running contract (authority) | `docs/13-ordarium-action-contract.md` §11 \\\"增量观测（ORD-BOOT-0）\\\" | `changes(filter?, cursor?)` reads committed revisions 跨主体 by **持久账本提交观测序**; ordering authority is the `ordarium_state_changes` metadata table written **in the same CAS transaction**; `written_at` and implicit `rowid` explicitly disqualified as clock/identity; cursor opaque, **global/filter-independent** |\\n| Goal/acceptance authority | `docs/17-ordarium-goals-and-accept",
